TTYCHATTER(1)              User Commands              TTYCHATTER(1)

NAME
    ttychatter - file-based OpenRouter chat client

SYNOPSIS
    ttychatter [options] input.txt output.log
    ttychatter --set-api-key [--gpg]
    ttychatter --forget-api-key
    ttychatter --models [--search TEXT] [--model-type TYPE]
    ttychatter --update-models
    ttychatter --test-model MODEL
    ttychatter --doctor
    ttychatter --version
    ttychatter --help

DESCRIPTION
    ttychatter is the C command-line client in the ttychatter family.
    It is not an ncurses interface.  It follows the traditional Unix file
    workflow: the user prepares an input file, invokes ttychatter, and the AI
    response is appended to an output/session file.

    The output file is also the session log.  Reusing the same output file
    resumes the conversation because ttychatter reads recent turns from that
    file and sends them as context.

BASIC USE
    Create an input prompt:

        cat > input.txt
        Explain what DNS caching means.
        ^D

    Send it and append the response to a session file:

        ttychatter input.txt session.log

    Continue the same session with a new input file:

        vi followup.txt
        ttychatter followup.txt session.log

API KEY SETUP
    The recommended first step is API-key setup.

    Store the OpenRouter API key encrypted with GPG:

        ttychatter --set-api-key --gpg

    Store the OpenRouter API key in plaintext config:

        ttychatter --set-api-key

    Plaintext storage is convenient but less safe.  Encrypted GPG storage uses
    the external gpg command and stores the key at API_KEY_GPG_FILE.

    Environment variables are also supported:

        OPENROUTER_API_KEY
        TTYCHATTER_API_KEY

CONFIGURATION
    Default config file:

        ~/.config/ttychatter/config

    Common keys:

        OPENROUTER_API_KEY
            Plaintext API key.  Environment variables override this.

        API_KEY_GPG_FILE
            Path to encrypted API key file.
            Default: ~/.config/ttychatter/api-key.gpg

        MODEL
            OpenRouter model/router.
            Default: openrouter/auto

        CONTEXT_TURNS
            Recent user/assistant turns read from the output log and sent as
            conversation context.
            Default: 12

        MODEL_CACHE_FILE
            OpenRouter model catalog cache.
            Default: ~/.cache/ttychatter/models.json

        SESSION_DIR
            Default session directory for other ttychatter clients.
            The C client can still write to any output file given on the
            command line.

        ATTACHMENT_DIR
            Directory for extracted code-block attachments.
            Default: ~/.local/share/ttychatter/attachments

        CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES
            Minimum line count before a returned fenced code block is saved as
            an attachment rather than left inline.
            Default: 5

        MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES
            Maximum local attachment size for inline sending.
            Default: 1048576

MODEL CATALOG
    Refresh the OpenRouter model cache:

        ttychatter --update-models

    List cached models:

        ttychatter --models

    Search cached models:

        ttychatter --models --search llama

    Show only routers or free models:

        ttychatter --models --model-type routers
        ttychatter --models --model-type free

    Recognized model types:

        all
        routers
        fixed
        free
        auto

MODEL TESTING
    Test one model without appending to a session log:

        ttychatter --test-model openrouter/auto

    The test sends a short availability prompt to the selected model and prints
    the raw response.

ATTACHMENTS
    Attach one or more files:

        ttychatter -a notes.txt input.txt session.log
        ttychatter -a notes.txt -a diagram.png input.txt session.log

    Text-like attachments are inserted into the user message as text.  Image
    attachments are sent as data URLs using OpenRouter's chat-completions
    content-part format when the selected model supports image input.

    Other binary files are listed in the prompt but not embedded as raw data in
    this first release.

LOOPBACK
    To also print the AI response to stdout:

        ttychatter --loopback input.txt session.log

    This is useful for pipes:

        ttychatter --loopback input.txt session.log | less

SESSION FORMAT
    The output file is human-readable and structured with markers:

        ===== TTYCHATTER TURN BEGIN =====
        ----- USER BEGIN -----
        ...
        ----- USER END -----
        ----- AI BEGIN -----
        ...
        ----- AI END -----
        ===== TTYCHATTER TURN END =====

    These markers allow ttychatter to reconstruct recent context later.

WALKTHROUGH
    A detailed step-by-step guide is provided in the WALKTHROUGH file included
    with the source distribution.

DIAGNOSTICS
    Show local diagnostics:

        ttychatter --doctor

    The doctor command reports config paths, API-key loading status, GPG
    availability, cache path, storage paths, and libcurl version.  It does not
    print API-key values.

FILES
    ~/.config/ttychatter/config
        Configuration file.

    ~/.config/ttychatter/api-key.gpg
        Default encrypted API key file.

    ~/.cache/ttychatter/models.json
        Cached OpenRouter model catalog.

    ~/.local/share/ttychatter/attachments
        Extracted code-block attachments.

LIMITATIONS
    - Requires libcurl and json-c.
    - GPG encryption requires the external gpg command.
    - Image attachment support depends on the selected model.
    - Non-image binary attachments are not fully embedded in this first C CLI
      release.
    - The command-line C client is intentionally not an ncurses UI.

VERSION
    ttychatter 0.1.0-c-cli

